{"question": "scr-decision-reactor", "strategy": "lean", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "effort": null, "answer": {"answer": "The default is set in scrapy/settings/default_settings.py (TWISTED_REACTOR = \"twisted.internet.asyncioreactor.AsyncioSelectorReactor\", line 609, alongside TWISTED_REACTOR_ENABLED = True). The docs explain it is the default because it enables native asyncio support, letting users use asyncio and asyncio-powered libraries in any coroutine with no extra setup. The release notes record the change from None to the asyncio reactor as a backward-incompatible change: newly generated projects had used this value since Scrapy 2.7.0 (via the startproject template), and the default was changed so that existing projects that do not set it explicitly also use the asyncio reactor (gh 6659, 6713). Users whose code does not work with it can switch to a different reactor or None.", "items": ["scrapy/settings/default_settings.py"], "evidence": ["scrapy/settings/default_settings.py:608-609", "docs/news.rst:3114-3121", "docs/topics/asyncio.rst:7-10", "docs/topics/asyncio.rst:21-27", "docs/topics/asyncio.rst:356-359", "docs/topics/settings.rst:2305-2310"]}, "outcome": "answered", "turns": 6, "tool_calls": 5, "tool_errors": 0, "context_chars": 26419, "seconds": 40.884, "usage": {"total_tokens": 45369}, "repo": "scrapy", "topic": "decisions", "category": "docs", "grade": {"score": 1.0, "precision": null, "recall": null, "missing": [], "extra": []}, "traceability": 1.0, "calls": ["search", "read_file", "read_file", "read_file", "read_file", "submit_answer"], "config": {"runner": "subagent", "max_turns": 25, "strategies": ["lean"], "questions": "bench/questions/scrapy.json", "repos": {"basic-python-cli": "d0379bb", "kg": "1a342c4", "kg-stale": "1a342c4", "my_first_data_project": "3d57177", "python-clean-architecture": "6f58de5", "scrapy": "8026dee"}, "kg": "kg 0.2.0", "kg_commit": "c0cc05a"}}
