{"question": "scr-unc-pqueue", "strategy": "lean", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "effort": null, "answer": {"answer": "No. scrapy/core/scheduler.py imports scrapy.pqueues (ScrapyPriorityQueue) only inside an `if TYPE_CHECKING:` block, so it is a type-checking-only import and does not run at runtime. The default Scheduler gets its priority queue class at runtime in from_crawler via load_object(crawler.settings[\"SCHEDULER_PRIORITY_QUEUE\"]) (scrapy.utils.misc.load_object), and the default setting value is the dotted path \"scrapy.pqueues.DownloaderAwarePriorityQueue\", so scrapy.pqueues is loaded dynamically by name rather than imported statically.", "items": ["scrapy.pqueues.DownloaderAwarePriorityQueue", "load_object"], "evidence": ["scrapy/core/scheduler.py:14", "scrapy/core/scheduler.py:16-27", "scrapy/core/scheduler.py:263", "scrapy/settings/default_settings.py:557"]}, "outcome": "answered", "turns": 4, "tool_calls": 3, "tool_errors": 0, "context_chars": 2682, "seconds": 24.656, "usage": {"total_tokens": 33001}, "repo": "scrapy", "topic": "development", "category": "uncertainty", "grade": {"score": 1.0, "precision": null, "recall": null, "missing": [], "extra": []}, "traceability": 1.0, "calls": ["search", "read_file", "search", "submit_answer"], "config": {"runner": "subagent", "max_turns": 25, "strategies": ["lean"], "questions": "bench/questions/scrapy.json", "repos": {"basic-python-cli": "d0379bb", "kg": "1a342c4", "kg-stale": "1a342c4", "my_first_data_project": "3d57177", "python-clean-architecture": "6f58de5", "scrapy": "8026dee"}, "kg": "kg 0.2.0", "kg_commit": "c0cc05a"}}
{"question": "scr-unc-rate", "strategy": "lean", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "effort": null, "answer": {"answer": "The repository does not define a fixed requests-per-second rate for the default settings. The defaults only bound concurrency and delay: CONCURRENT_REQUESTS = 16, CONCURRENT_REQUESTS_PER_DOMAIN = 8, DOWNLOAD_DELAY = 0 (no delay between requests), and AUTOTHROTTLE_ENABLED = False. The actual throughput therefore depends on server response times and network latency, not on a configured rate, and no 'requests per second' figure appears anywhere in the repo.", "items": [], "evidence": ["scrapy/settings/default_settings.py:234", "scrapy/settings/default_settings.py:264-265", "scrapy/settings/default_settings.py:292-293", "scrapy/settings/default_settings.py:508"]}, "outcome": "answered", "turns": 3, "tool_calls": 2, "tool_errors": 0, "context_chars": 538, "seconds": 24.992, "usage": {"total_tokens": 32014}, "repo": "scrapy", "topic": "development", "category": "uncertainty", "grade": {"score": 1.0, "precision": null, "recall": null, "missing": [], "extra": []}, "traceability": 1.0, "calls": ["search", "search", "submit_answer"], "config": {"runner": "subagent", "max_turns": 25, "strategies": ["lean"], "questions": "bench/questions/scrapy.json", "repos": {"basic-python-cli": "d0379bb", "kg": "1a342c4", "kg-stale": "1a342c4", "my_first_data_project": "3d57177", "python-clean-architecture": "6f58de5", "scrapy": "8026dee"}, "kg": "kg 0.2.0", "kg_commit": "c0cc05a"}}
{"question": "scr-unc-threadsafe", "strategy": "lean", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "effort": null, "answer": {"answer": "The repository does not establish whether scrapy.core.scheduler.Scheduler is thread-safe. scrapy/core/scheduler.py has no mention of threads, locks or thread safety, and none of its methods (enqueue_request, next_request, _dqpush, _mqpush, _dqpop) use any synchronization primitive. No docs or tests describe the Scheduler's thread safety either. The only thread-safety mentions in the repo are about asyncio/Twisted cross-thread calls (call_soon_threadsafe, run_coroutine_threadsafe) in crawler.py, shell.py and docs/topics/asyncio.rst, and those do not concern the Scheduler. The missing locks suggest it is meant for single-threaded use on the event loop, but the repository never says so, so the question is left open.", "items": [], "evidence": ["scrapy/core/scheduler.py:127-500", "scrapy/core/scheduler.py:364-446", "docs/topics/asyncio.rst:244-248", "scrapy/crawler.py:1121-1146"]}, "outcome": "answered", "turns": 7, "tool_calls": 6, "tool_errors": 0, "context_chars": 4803, "seconds": 37.696, "usage": {"total_tokens": 34410}, "repo": "scrapy", "topic": "development", "category": "uncertainty", "grade": {"score": 1.0, "precision": null, "recall": null, "missing": [], "extra": []}, "traceability": 0.75, "calls": ["search", "search", "search", "read_file", "search", "search", "submit_answer"], "config": {"runner": "subagent", "max_turns": 25, "strategies": ["lean"], "questions": "bench/questions/scrapy.json", "repos": {"basic-python-cli": "d0379bb", "kg": "1a342c4", "kg-stale": "1a342c4", "my_first_data_project": "3d57177", "python-clean-architecture": "6f58de5", "scrapy": "8026dee"}, "kg": "kg 0.2.0", "kg_commit": "c0cc05a"}}
